// Research Desk demo: Archivist agent (ABI structured-v1).
//
// Sits on the escalation gate's completed route (gate -> archive -> out), so it
// sees exactly the values a human released: a null-payload approve preserves the
// team's best-effort record (for an escalated run, the sentinel refusal), and a
// non-null approve payload REPLACES the released value -- that replacement is the
// human's own answer. Model output can never reach this node: the accept path
// (decide -> out) bypasses it by topology.
//
// Archive condition, checked structurally (a malformed human payload must never
// error the deploy, so no method is called on an unvalidated value): the input is
// a map carrying a non-empty string question and a non-empty string answer whose
// first 20 characters are not the INSUFFICIENT CONTEXT sentinel. Exactly then a
// Q&A document is filed into embers-demo-docs (idempotent create, then upsert
// keyed "qa: " ++ question, so re-answering a question overwrites its entry).
// Recognized records return with an added "archived": true|false field; anything
// else passes through unchanged (a non-map has nowhere to carry a flag).
//
// Replay note: rho:chroma:collection:entries:new is NOT replay-cached -- it
// re-executes during replay validation -- and rho:chroma:collection:new is called
// with ignoreOrUpdateIfExists = true; both are idempotent insert-or-overwrite
// operations keyed by collection and document id, so replay is result-
// deterministic. On observer nodes both are NoOp and ack silently.
//
// Infra failure (Chroma down on the validator) surfaces as a deploy error ->
// disposition failed; the archive node's retry policy in the team definition
// absorbs it with bounded backoff.
contract main(@invocation, return) = {
  new createCollection(`rho:chroma:collection:new`),
      upsertEntries(`rho:chroma:collection:entries:new`),
      createdCh, seededCh in {
    match invocation.getOrElse("input", Nil) {
      record => {
        match record {
          {"question": question /\ String, "answer": answer /\ String, ..._} => {
            if (answer.length() >= 20 and answer.slice(0, 20) == "INSUFFICIENT CONTEXT") {
              // Null-payload approve preserved the refusal. The desk must not
              // learn its own refusal.
              return!({"output": record.set("archived", false), "disposition": "completed"})
            } else {
              if (question.length() > 0 and answer.length() > 0) {
                createCollection!("embers-demo-docs", true, {"purpose": "embers-research-desk-demo"}, *createdCh) |
                for (_ <- createdCh) {
                  upsertEntries!(
                    "embers-demo-docs",
                    {("qa: " ++ question): ("Q: " ++ question ++ "\nA: " ++ answer, {"source": "human-approval", "topic": "qa"})},
                    *seededCh
                  ) |
                  for (_ <- seededCh) {
                    return!({"output": record.set("archived", true), "disposition": "completed"})
                  }
                }
              } else {
                return!({"output": record.set("archived", false), "disposition": "completed"})
              }
            }
          }
          _ => {
            // Not the record shape (including non-map payloads): pass through
            // untouched and unarchived.
            return!({"output": record, "disposition": "completed"})
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
